## Gaps

- useBookingFlow: index previously noted it doesn't exist. Confirmed: the multi-step booking flow logic lives in ChatController.php (session management with PROMPT_VERSION, cache keys with 15-min TTL) and RequestSettingsService (shared to frontend via HandleInertiaRequests). No dedicated `use-booking-flow.ts` hook exists; the chatbot derives booking window options and minAdvanceDays from RequestSettingsService::all() shared as `requestOptions` page prop.

- route('chat.stream') now registered: confirmed registered in routes/web.php line 190-196 under Route::prefix('/chat')->group. The frontend in chatService.ts line 121 calls route('chat.stream') for streaming connections.

- OpenRouterClient naming vs NVIDIA provider: class name is OpenRouterClient but configured provider is NVIDIA (config/ai.php: provider => 'nvidia'). The model defaults to nvidia_nim/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b. The testCsrf endpoint reports 'provider' => 'nvidia' and 'configured_model' => 'nvidia_nim/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b'. Naming mismatch remains: class says "OpenRouter" but actual provider is NVIDIA.

- RuleIndexingService: NOT a stub. Functional service at app/Services/RAG/RuleIndexingService.php that indexes rule embeddings into pgvector when both embedding model is configured AND database driver is pgsql. Checks useVectorSearch() which requires embedder->isConfigured() && config('database.default') === 'pgsql'. Dispatches via IndexRuleEmbedding job from RulesController. Falls back to priority-ordered rule selection when vector search is not available.

- resources/js/layout.tsx/default..tsx: typo in task description. Real path is resources/js/layout.tsx/default.tsx. Contains DefaultLayout component with sidebar, breadcrumbs, theme toggle, and Chatbot inclusion.

- page_context / get_page_context usage: used in ChatController.php getContextAwareSystemPrompt() method (line 242) as a tool available to the AI. Frontend calls route('api.page.context') to fetch page context from PageContextController at /api/page-context. The tool is injected into the AI's system prompt and available via get_page_context function call. Also used in resources/js/components/chatbot/utils/pageContext.ts (client-side collection) and resources/js/lib/useCurrentPageContext.ts (React hook).

- Chat session cache keys: chat_session_{user_id}, chat_faq_state_{user_id} with 15-minute TTL, plus PROMPT_VERSION prefix (v2) for automatic invalidation on deploy.

- No dedicated booking flow hook: the chatbot guided flow uses RequestSettingsService data (booking window, min advance days) shared as `requestOptions` page prop, not a separate useBookingFlow hook.

